ruff
# golang: needed directly, not just as a lint-tool dependency — the
# setup-claude-code bootstrap step `go install`s claude-statusline (the Claude
# Code status line), which has no Fedora package.
golang
golangci-lint
golang-x-tools-goimports

# Window Manager / Desktop
niri
hyprlock
noctalia-shell
# sddm: the display manager. Fedora 44's KDE spin ships plasma-login-manager
# instead, but this machine runs niri, not Plasma — and the whole Plasma stack
# is removed by the setup-deplasma step. sddm is the greeter Juliet themes
# (etc/sddm-themes/juliet, applied by setup-sddm). sddm-wayland-generic
# provides the Wayland session support sddm needs to launch niri.
sddm
sddm-wayland-generic
# keyd: system-level key remapper. Used to give leftmeta (Super) a dual role —
# hold = the Mod modifier for niri, tap = F13 (bound to the noctalia menu).
# Configured by the setup-keyd bootstrap step (/etc/keyd/default.conf).
keyd
fuzzel
rofimoji
# lxqt-policykit: the polkit authentication agent niri spawns at startup (see
# the spawn-at-startup line in niri/config.kdl). A bare compositor starts no
# agent, so without it polkit prompts never appear. polkit-gnome — the usual
# choice in sway/hyprland guides — was retired from Fedora, and Plasma's
# polkit-kde only runs inside a Plasma session.
lxqt-policykit
# bolt: Thunderbolt device authorization daemon (boltd/boltctl). This XPS 15
# 9500 has a Thunderbolt controller at security level "user", meaning devices
# must be authorized before they work at all. bolt arrived as a dependency of
# plasma-thunderbolt (the Plasma GUI for it) and left with it; the daemon
# itself is DE-agnostic and is what actually does the authorizing.
bolt
wl-clipboard
cliphist
playerctl
brightnessctl
pavucontrol

